<title>AUSTRALIA: Long Australian bonds sag as U.S. weighs on market.</title>
<headline>Long Australian bonds sag as U.S. weighs on market.</headline>
<text>
<p>----------(Snapshot at 4.35 P.M./0635 GMT)------------------</p>
<p>FUTURES					  CASH YIELD</p>
<p>90-DAY BILLS  (SEP) 95.08    (unch)     4.93   (- 0.02)</p>
<p>3-YR T-BONDS  (SEP) 94.29  (- 0.01)     5.55     (unch)</p>
<p>10-YR T-BONDS (SEP) 93.495 (-0.055)     6.53   (+ 0.06)</p>
<p>AUD/USD  0.7355 (PREV 0.7392) US 30-YR  6.51   (6.49 NY)</p>
<p>---------------------(Aug 6)--------------------------------</p>
<p>*Australian bonds end in negative territory after uninspired day dominated by softer U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>*Market waiting on labour force data on Thursday. Treasury Assistant Secretary Hinton speaks in Sydney later on Wednesday.</p>
